  "interpretation": "In this deterministic filtered screen ordinary recurrence rounding exceeds same-state accumulation rounding by the recorded aggregate RMS ratio. Among sequential setup substitutions, geometry has the largest aggregate sensitivity (9.00e-4 relative RMS), followed by f32 paired recurrence factors (1.51e-4), sectoral seed (2.18e-5), and coefficient preparation (1.95e-6). Geometry sensitivity peaks near polar rings; at equator ring 360 geometry is exact for this grid, while factor and coefficient-preparation sensitivities are locally material. These are one-at-a-time sensitivities, not additive error components. The probe is not an independent DUCC accuracy or performance result.",
  "method": {
    "accumulation_reference": "Accumulate the observed f32 recurrence states times the exact prepared f32 even/odd coefficients in f64, then combine using the same f32 cosine widened to f64.",
    "candidate_replay": "The exact f32 paired recurrence and fused sums are independently replayed from prepared f32 factors; the replayed north value is bitwise equal to the candidate SIMD batch for all observations.",
    "prefix": "The f32 initializer is advanced through the observed initial rescale/restore; selected observations remain in the ordinary suffix with no scaled pair recurrence.",
    "recurrence_reference": "Replay the recurrence in f64 using the same corrected f32 starting value, f32 A/B factors, f32 cosine-squared value, and f32 prepared even/odd coefficients widened to f64.",
    "setup_sensitivities": "Sequential one-at-a-time f64 substitutions: first f32 recurrence factors to f64 factors; then f32 cosine/cosine-squared to f64 grid geometry; then f32 sectoral seed to f64 sin^m and normalization; then f32 prepared coefficient pairs to f64 prepared pairs. Each sensitivity is the change from the immediately preceding replay and the contributions are not an additive error budget."
